I found "yet" to be quite unnecessary.

So there I was, my fourth game on NAO. I had absolutely NO idea that
I'd actually ascend this time. The farthest I got before was killed by
a minotaur at 100k points. It wasn't particularly lucky or unlucky.
The RNG seemed almost... passive. It ignored me, pretty much. 'Till
once when I slipped and mocked the mysterious force as a lawful
samurai -not recommended-. So the RNG decided I should do Asmodeus's
lair 6 times.

It started normally, as any game should. Actually it ended normally
too. The whole thing was normal. "Oh my God, I didn't find a randomly
generated wand of wishing! OH NO!" Two magic lamps provided me with my
first two wishes, followed by the castle wand for the last six wishes
I ever used. Yup, 0:2. I descended as normal, going through the
gnomish mines and not picking up the luckstone. Why? I had one. I
didn't find out until deep into Gehennom that it was just a
flintstone. Out came the Tsurugi of Muramasa. Sokoban --> Mines -->
Medusa --> Quest --> Gehennom --> altar camped --> More Gehennom -->
looked for Vlad --> Found VS --> Killed Rodney --> Got the Amulet --
> ???? --> Profit!

Vlad's had two amulet of life saving. Add that to the one I found in
Rodney's tower, and the one I wished for, that makes four, none of
which I ended up using. Huge waste of a wish. Should've gone with some
non-shitty helmet or another magic marker.

On Dlvl 15, There were no exits, no secret doors, and no stairs. After
searching for probably a thousand turns or so, a dwarf shows up and
starts mining. Oh, yeah! Free pickaxe! I thought. Hachi, GO!
Unfortunately, the dwarf killed my poor dog. I got pissed (usually a
bad thing to do in NetHack, not this time) and dishonourably attacked
the dwarf. I was still mad, so I repeatedly quaffed from a sink,
hoping for some random death. Nope. Polymorphed into a female and
every single stat increased. "Grognor is mollified". Kickass.

A wizard bones gave me CoMR, and Sokoban nicely game me an AoR. Then I
found a magic lamp. I had already created Excalibur and Snickersnee at
this point, soo... crap. I wished for SDSM and ditched the amulet.
Mistake! Don't do this! Keep the cloak slot in favor of the amulet
slot! Eventually I got pissed again because I kept falling into water
and quaffed an unID'd potion. Polymorph. I merged with my silver
scales and found killer bees to be delicious. Got a ton of royal jelly
there, but I lost my CoMR. The Castle wand gave me another one.

I spent at least three hours just deciding what to wish for at
different points. And I'm never wishing for a "oLS again.

f - a wand of indecision (1:2)

I found a huge number of wands of death in this game. None of which I
actually needed. (Well, Ashikaga might have bisected me without, so
blah. I had a wand of sleep anyway.) The Wizard of Yendor didn't put
up a fight at ALL, and he only attacked me four times. I wish it was
more because once I passed Gehennom it seemed a little... TOO easy. I
killed famine entirely with a ring of conflict. Twice. Pestilence went
down with a single death charge (okay, useful, but unnecessary). and
his was the correct altar. I actually considered just hanging out on
Astral, knowing nothing could kill me, but decided against it. The
invisible choir sang, and I was bathed in radiance. Did I want my
possessions identified? y

I could type a lot more, but I have a massive headache.

